<section class="wrap section section--tight">
  <div class="cal-box" id="calendar">
    <div class="cal-box__intro">
      <svg class="cal-box__icon" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="6" y="10" width="36" height="32" rx="5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/>
        <path d="M6 19h36M16 6v8M32 6v8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path d="M17 30l5 5 9-10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
      <div>
        <h2 class="cal-box__title">Put our events in your calendar</h2>
        <p class="cal-box__lede">All our talks and outings can appear in the calendar on your phone, tablet or computer. When we add a new event, it will appear in your calendar by itself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="cal-box__prompt">Which calendar do you use?</p>
    <div class="cal-box__options">
      <a class="cal-option" href="<%= calendar.apple %>">
        <span class="cal-option__name">iPhone, iPad or Mac</span>
        <span class="cal-option__hint">The Calendar app from Apple</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cal-option" href="<%= calendar.google %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="cal-option__name">Google Calendar</span>
        <span class="cal-option__hint">Used on most Android phones</span>
      </a>
      <a class="cal-option" href="<%= calendar.outlook %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="cal-option__name">Outlook</span>
        <span class="cal-option__hint">Including Hotmail and Live</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <details class="cal-box__more">
      <summary>What happens when I press one of these?</summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Your calendar will open and ask if you'd like to add <strong>Beckenham &amp; Bromley HA events</strong>. Press <strong>Subscribe</strong> or <strong>Add</strong> to say yes.</li>
        <li>Google and Outlook may ask you to sign in first, using the same details you normally use for your email.</li>
        <li>That's all. Our events will then show in your calendar alongside your own, and new ones will be added by themselves.</li>
        <li>If you change your mind, you can remove <strong>Beckenham &amp; Bromley HA events</strong> from your calendar's list of calendars at any time. It won't affect anything else.</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details class="cal-box__more">
      <summary>Use a different calendar?</summary>
      <p>Most calendars have an option to add a calendar "from the internet" or "by web address". Copy this address and paste it in there:</p>
      <div class="cal-box__copy">
        <input type="text" value="<%= calendar.feed %>" readonly aria-label="Calendar web address" data-copy-source>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--outline" data-copy>Copy</button>
      </div>
      <p class="muted">Or <a href="<%= calendar.download %>">download our events as a calendar file</a>. (A downloaded file won't update by itself, so you'd need to download it again for new events.)</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
